<title>ITALY: Italy has already reached 3 pct EMU goal - Veltroni.</title>
<headline>Italy has already reached 3 pct EMU goal - Veltroni.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy has already reached the three percent deficit/GDP Maastricht goal for early entry to the single European currency, deputy Prime Minister Walter Veltroni said.</p>
<p>He was commenting on an earlier statement by state auditor Andrea Monorchio who said he was convinced Italy would reach the three percent goal by the end of this year.</p>
<p>&quot;We are already at three percent and forecasts are for a further positive performance,&quot; Veltroni told reporters while attending a congress of the CISL union confederation.</p>
<p>&quot;All the data available to use shows that we are coming out of the tunnel and that economic fundamentals are back on track.</p>
<p>&quot;We can really reckon that the second part of this year will be one of recovery,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
